block head
    title Vaginitis - Plants Cause Disease

block content
    h1 Vaginitis
    p Definition by #[a(href="https://www.mayoclinic.org/diseases-conditions/vaginitis/symptoms-causes/syc-20354707") Mayo Clinic]:
    blockquote Vaginitis is an inflammation of the vagina that can result in discharge, itching and pain. The cause is usually a change in the balance of vaginal bacteria or an infection. Reduced estrogen levels after menopause and some skin disorders also can cause vaginitis.
